{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/314862-krampus-in-ctl","id":314862,"title":"Krampus in CtL","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-17T15:42:23-08:00","id":314862,"title":"Krampus in CtL","content":"I prepare Christmas themed one-shot adventure in what I want to use the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Krampus\" target=\"_blank\">Krampus</a> from Alpine folklore. I now think what powers should he have? Should it be True Fea, or just hobgoblin? What is difference in interpreting the myths?<br /> <br /> Seeing as Krampus is stealing children, maybe better is to go with True Fae road?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T16:50:30-08:00","id":314932,"title":"","content":"I'd make him a Gentry with a bit more of a habit of visiting earth than usual.<br /> <br /> One option could be he has his own (insane) roster of which Gentry has been good/friends/whatevs and he drops off stolen children with them rather than being anyone's keeper. You could have several changelings stolen by Krampus with different keepers then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T19:29:21-08:00","id":315009,"title":"","content":"How to make a stats for True Fae? Should it have Seeming? Because Krampus looks for me a lot like Beast, I think...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/314862-krampus-in-ctl?p=314932#post314932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One option could be he has his own (insane) roster of which Gentry has been good/friends/whatevs and he drops off stolen children with them rather than being anyone's keeper. You could have several changelings stolen by Krampus with different keepers then.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would rather make him <b>compete</b> with mine PCs Keeper. As my players are under Arcadian Huntsman care, I think interesting would be that he want's to hunt for the Krampus himself - biggest prey is to get Gentry itself, don't it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> - so he need his own changelings to lure Krampus out. To make it more devious for my players, they Arcadian Huntsman will only made them to lure out human the Huntsman think Krampus will want to kidnap. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Hobgoblen or perhaps a very old and powerful Scarecrow Minister would work best in that interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is Scarecrow Minister?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T01:40:46-08:00","id":315193,"title":"","content":"Scarecrow Ministry is a Entitlement in <b>Changeling: The Lost</b><br /> Generally stating Gentry is in <b>Autumn Nightmares</b>, but <b>Equinox Road</b> fleshes out what they really are. Depending on how deep in Changeling mythos you want to take it the info in ER may or may not be relevant to you","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T05:03:55-08:00","id":315272,"title":"","content":"Its a Title of the same True Fae as Santa. The stories about Santa &amp; the Krampus are roughly true - except for the EVERY (Christian) girl and boy part. Most children just get store bought gifts from their parents, otherwise the world would actually be aware of the strange toys showing up in everyone's houses. In fact, Santa just delivers his wonderous toys to a very select list every year, and the Krampus carries off a select list of naughty children. Those children of course toil away into Wizened in Santa's workshop in Arcadia, and are his elves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T04:39:27-08:00","id":318162,"title":"","content":"Here is my own version of child and adults stealing Krampus as True Fae. Stats are for him on Earth, not Arcadia \u2013 so are made as changeling, using GMC update. Still, I need for him power to sense sins in people and to go through chimneys... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Isn\u2019t he a bit overpowered, compared to other Fae? Feel free to comment or advise. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:22px\"><b><i>Krampus</i></b></span></div> <br /> <img src=\"http://s6843.chomikuj.pl/ChomikImage.aspx?e=rmV034_YzAT0lVfe3MiI3Ttu9gnsu_s639QIR2_2vktC5wnRkNcZ2P297D4vAWm1DS6Fm1wI1Io_rQwvI1uVuJhw9H6u1eJypOC5sMLH05s&amp;pv=2\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b>Seeming: </b>Beast<br /> <b>Kith: </b>Broadback \u2013 most images of his are black faun, goat-like figure<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Justice<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Greed<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes: </b>Intelligence 4, Wits 5, Resolve 6<br /> <b>Physical Attributes: </b>Strength 6, Dexterity 5, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes: </b>Presence 5, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Crafts 2, Investigation (Sins) 5. Occult 1, Politics 1<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 5, Brawl 4, Larceny 3, Stealth 4, Survival 4<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken (Goats) 3, Intimidation ( Children) 5, Persuasion 2, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <br /> <b>Merits: </b>Danger Sense 2, Charmed Life 2, Lethal Mein 2<br /> <b>Contracts:</b> Darkness 3, Den 3, Oath and Punishment 2, Omen 1, Wild 4<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 9<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 8<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 16<br /> <b>Health:</b> 10<br /> <b>Wyrd:</b> 6<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://s7471.chomikuj.pl/ChomikImage.aspx?e=bGHKpiazwP-fNXNopV-MVfiKeQU4ZeiYH-FT9qGDhQnAk7nrz9EeuGod0EoLRCacyXbRphBC2HF83LCXq5y_hAujnNWtnH0B-6cKiD-io2o&amp;pv=2\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <b>Blessings:</b><br /> <b>Beast: </b>Karmpus have 8 again rule when using the Animal Ken Skill.<br /> Krampus can spend points of Glamour to add to dice pools involving Presence and Composure. Each point of Glamour spent adds one die to one dice pool.<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmare Aura: </b>All within 50 yards of the Fae find their Speed cut in half (round down).<br /> <br /> <b>Stoic Forbearance: </b>Krampus can spend one point of Glamour to add two to all dice pools involving Stamina, for the rest of scene<br /> <br /> <b>Curses:</b><br /> Karmpus suffers a \u20134 dice untrained penalty when trying to use a Mental skill in which the character has no dots.<br /> Krampus doesn\u2019t re-roll 10s when using a dice pool involving Intelligence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-21-2014, 07:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T09:31:05-08:00","id":350699,"title":"","content":"I read the <b>Equinox Road</b> now it got me on interesting idea to think about on <b>GlamourWeaver</b>'s answer:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/314862-krampus-in-ctl?p=315272#post315272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its a Title of the same True Fae as Santa. The stories about Santa &amp; the Krampus are roughly true - except for the EVERY (Christian) girl and boy part. Most children just get store bought gifts from their parents, otherwise the world would actually be aware of the strange toys showing up in everyone's houses. In fact, Santa just delivers his wonderous toys to a very select list every year, and the Krampus carries off a select list of naughty children. Those children of course toil away into Wizened in Santa's workshop in Arcadia, and are his elves.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Krampus is second Actor of the True Fae the Santa is? Or maybe he is his Nemesis? See below:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equinox Road</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Nemesis:</b> Some Kindly Ones have living reflections. They\u2019re perfect opposites, fiery where the original is cold and loving where she\u2019s hateful, near-duplicates who copy their sisters down to the last Title and personality trait or something in between. An entity like this is a Nemesis: a potent danger to a Fae\u2019s immortal existence. Despite what a typical faerie would like to believe, a Nemesis isn\u2019t an imperfect, week counterpart, but a genuine Fae, equal in power and privilege. Educated changelings note the resemblance to their own fetches, so some believe there\u2019s a relationship. They say the Others learned eldritch secrets from their twins and used them to craft their slaves\u2019 stand-ins.<br /> <br /> No matter what appearance it takes, a Nemesis has the same true name as its enemy. It\u2019s an independent, alternate identity with its own will and desires, tied to the same foundation as its twin. If one swears a namebound oath, its obligations and benefits applies to both of them. If one loses its name, they both suffer the consequences. This doesn\u2019t apply to Titles, however. One might have more or different Titles than the other, and Titlebound Contracts don\u2019t transfer between them. When one of them loses a Title, the other one isn\u2019t affected.<br /> <br /> A True Fae\u2019s Nemesis often fights its twin for power over their shared name. Titles offer no protection; the<br /> Nemesis has no obligation to devour them in turn before assailing her enemy\u2019s name because it\u2019s her name, too. This makes the Nemesis more dangerous than any other Fae the \u201coriginal\u201d might encounter. She\u2019s just getting rid of the \u201cextra\u201d will. When one wins, the other\u2019s obliterated.<br /> <br /> Most Fae don\u2019t have Nemeses \u2014 or don\u2019t know they have them. A Nemesis doesn\u2019t always spring into existencewhen his twin\u2019s born. They say Nemeses can erupt part of the way through an immortal\u2019s life, born of malformed oaths or malefic rituals.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the question is shuold Santa and Krampus be one True Fae or two, oposite ones Gentry? But this idea of Krampus stealing naughty people for Santa as his Wizined elves is sooooo much tasty..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T19:42:15-07:00","id":1140066,"title":"","content":"Krampus: the Yule Lord by Brom is an interesting take on the Santa &amp; Krampus legend. In Brom's story Krampus is the son of Loki and Santa is Balder back from the dead and living in disguise. Balder(Santa) sealed Krampus away a few hundred years ago but he has recently escaped. Santa lives in Spain in a castle not at the north pole. Krampus and Santa are fighting each other for control of Yule. It's a good read, I'm sure you can find ideas to put to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T22:46:31-07:00","id":1140089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/314862-krampus-in-ctl#post314862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prepare Christmas themed one-shot adventure in what I want to use the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Krampus\" target=\"_blank\">Krampus</a> from Alpine folklore. I now think what powers should he have? Should it be True Fea, or just hobgoblin? What is difference in interpreting the myths?<br /> <br /> Seeing as Krampus is stealing children, maybe better is to go with True Fae road?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would be cool if you did a Changeling Christmas Chronicle that introduced several spirits and ghouls associated with the that holiday like <span style=\"color:#040404\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Gryla</b> is an Ogress who lives in the mountains of Iceland, and </span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#040404\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Mari Lwyd</b>, a Welsh Zombie Horse that visits people's homes and pubs during the Christmas season. </span></span></span></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T23:00:59-07:00","id":1140092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/314862-krampus-in-ctl?p=315009#post315009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How to make a stats for True Fae? Should it have Seeming? Because Krampus looks for me a lot like Beast, I think...<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True Fae are reality warpers, they can appear however they want to, within the boundaries of their Titles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}